cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MOLRAPTOR: Molecular Learning via Rapid Processing of Topological Representations"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-07-20"
authors:
  - family-names: "Contreras-Torres"
    given-names: "Flavio F."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2375-131X"
    affiliation: "Tecnologico de Monterrey"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NanoBiostructuresRG/molraptor"
license: "LGPL-3.0-or-later"
abstract: >-
  MOLRAPTOR is a SMILES-first scientific library and command-line tool for
  generating reproducible binary Morgan fingerprints from user-provided
  molecular representations. It supports in-memory encoding and CSV/TXT
  workflows, preserves input order and duplicates, isolates invalid records,
  and records deterministic input and profile hashes with runtime metadata.
  MOLRAPTOR parses supplied SMILES with RDKit but does not retrieve, curate,
  harmonize, canonicalize, or replace them.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - molecular fingerprints
  - Morgan fingerprints
  - molecular representations
  - SMILES
  - RDKit
  - reproducible research
  - computational chemistry
